/-!
# F2b′'s successors with the piece, the tail start and the offset fixed (D57)

Packet PROVE-SB2-CANON, round 4 (decision D57). `Nd.SB2LowerStageVersionStatement5` (tails) and
`Ne.SB2LowerRootVersionStatement8` (root) leave the versions' piece `pc`, the tail start `tL` and the offset `x₀`
existential and unconstrained, while their consumers need them: SB2LIFT's P-level S2 clause `Sx.ae_isStageS2_tail`
takes `pc = pcPt (run ℓ) (E ℓ)`, `tL = 0` and `x₀` the right entry value (`IsRightEntryChart` of the retained union
`A ∪ B_{<ℓ}` at its right end), and the identification of the canonical driver needs the same normalization. The
successors below are the landed statements verbatim with these clauses added to the conclusion (PROVE-AUX61-NOJUMP
proves them from its construction: `Nc.StageObj` has all three):

* **`SB2LowerStageVersionStatement6`** (tails): Statement5 plus `∀ ω, pc ω = pcPt (run ℓ) (E ℓ ω)`, `∀ ω, tL ω = 0`,
  and, almost surely on `F`, `IsRightEntryChart X (realMax X) ((Mo.hullChart (fill X) 0).recenter (x₀ ω))` for
  `X = Nc.retX ℓ = A ∪ B_{<ℓ}` (exactly `Sx.ae_isStageS2_tail`'s `hpc`, `htL`, `hx₀`);
* **`SB2LowerRootVersionStatement9`** (root, `ℓ = relOff`): Statement8 (whose tail start is already `τE`) plus
  `∀ ω, pc ω = pcPt (run ℓ) (E ℓ ω)` and, almost surely on the root event `Fr`, the right entry clause at
  `R = realMax A`.

R48: no source theorem is assumed; these are named statements (owner PROVE-AUX61-NOJUMP, D57).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

noncomputable section

